    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0928" n="900" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v15/pg900"/>

                <head>503. Telegram From the Embassy in Egypt to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d503-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-07-25T19:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25, 1956—7
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>134. If Nasser announces termination Point IV and Embassy queried by press
                    propose reply unless otherwise instructed regretting decision terminate program
                    which had been so successful (listing achievements) but pointing out that ICA
                    programs and other forms US assistance operative only in countries where such
                    cooperation welcomed in efforts achieve common goals.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Byroade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
